  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/08b3898f8aa867bfec0453da33cc8ae2d1f222d65029f45f09bf0beccb1dca62.png)\n\nLet $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function $f(x)$ shown above. What is the mode of $X?$",
  "worked_solution": "The mode of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ is the value of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we can tell that $f(x)$ has a single global maximum at $x=12.$\n\nTherefore, the mode of $X$ is $12.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/ed9bc805045e01c7524fb32292b3728239432b9169bd1af148204804f9df700c.png)",
